# Forum post requirements

Apply these requirements whenever creating, replacing, or editing forum posts in `src/data/blogs.ts` and their media entries in `src/data/media.ts`.

## Voice and accuracy

- Write clear, direct English at an 8th- to 10th-grade reading level.
- Keep paragraphs to 1–4 sentences.
- Do not use the words `tapestry`, `testament`, `delve`, or `paramount`.
- Do not moralize. Describe Elytra and compatibility as technical systems whose behavior can change after updates.
- Never mention `zadeyo` or `Zadeyo` in article copy, metadata, image text, or replies.
- Verify time-sensitive game, platform, feature, and anti-cheat claims with reliable sources before writing.
- Never use the word `undetected` in article copy, metadata, image text, or replies. Describe compatibility and detection status as labels that can change after updates.

## SEO and structure

- Use the supplied title and primary keyword. Put the primary keyword in the first 100 words.
- Generate the slug from the primary keyword using no more than four words.
- Use exactly one H1 (the post title), then logical H2 and H3 headings without skipped levels.
- Use secondary keywords naturally and bold them sparingly.
- Classify the post:
  - Type 1, feature/commercial: link naturally to related feature or configuration threads.
  - Type 2, comparison: link each major compared feature to its dedicated thread when one exists.
  - Type 3, informational/guide: answer the query first and connect relevant feature threads to specific gameplay friction.
- Prevent keyword cannibalization between forum threads. Each post must stay focused on its unique primary keyword and search intent.
- Include the exact transactional phrase exactly once in the article body:
  `<a href="https://cheatsforwardogs.org/wardogs-cheats">Wardogs cheats</a>`
- The exact phrase may also occur in a supplied title when it is the primary keyword; the one-use limit applies to body copy.
- Finish with 4–5 useful FAQ entries whose answers are 2–4 concise sentences.
- Keep the existing strong purchase CTA rendered by `BlogPostPage.tsx`.

## Required image

- Every forum post must have exactly one visible still image.
- Assign the image in `FORUM_MEDIA` in `src/data/media.ts`.
- Use existing sequential assets: `image-1`, `image-2`, `image-3`, and so on.
- Rotate images in post order so adjacent posts do not use the same image when multiple assets exist.
- Add accurate alt text, title, and caption for the article topic.
- Keep the current responsive `SeoMedia` presentation.

## Required community replies

- Every post must define 4–5 natural entries in its `replies` array.
- Use distinct, plausible handles and a mix of short tips, personal observations, and genuine follow-up questions.
- Replies must discuss article details and must not read like repeated sales copy.
- Reply dates must be the publication date or later.
- Use optional roles only where they add context.

## Publishing checks

- Add new slugs to `FORUM_MEDIA` and `scripts/generate-sitemaps.mjs`.
- Update internal links and redirects when a slug replaces an older URL.
- Keep an existing thread live until its replacement is ready, then remove or redirect it in the same change.
- Run `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, and `npm run build`.
- Confirm generated sitemap and OG assets contain the new threads and no deleted thread URLs.
